@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Logging & ops alerts
+
+PegaFila splits observability into three lanes. Pick the lane first, then the API.
+
+| Lane | Channel / API | Where it goes | Retention | Use when |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::info/debug/warning/error(...)` (default `stack` → `daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (rotated daily) | 14 days (`LOG_DAILY_DAYS`) | Routine application logs: request handling, domain events, debug to error. This is the default — use it unless the event is an audit trail or a page. |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (rotated daily, min level `info`) | 90 days (`LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`) | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail: membership role changes, subscription transitions, login lockouts. Always include actor, entity, action, and outcome; never log secrets. |
+| **Alert** | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send($title, $message, $context)` | Discord incoming webhook (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`) | n/a (chat) | Human-pageable ops incidents only: a job that exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity. Code that decides an incident is worth waking someone up. |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. **Someone must act now?** → Alert via `DiscordOpsAlert`. Keep it rare, actionable, and redacted.
+2. **Must we prove later who did what?** → Audit via `Log::channel('audit')`. One line per state change or rejected attempt.
+3. **Otherwise** → Archive via `Log::` (default stack). Debug freely; it rotates away.
+
+## Rules
+
+- Discord is **never** a Monolog log channel. There is no `discord` channel in
+  `config/logging.php`. Alerts are an explicit `DiscordOpsAlert::send()` call.
+- `DiscordOpsAlert` never throws and never logs the webhook URL (it embeds the
+  token). Transport failures and non-2xx answers are recorded as `Log::error()`
+  entries without the URL.
+- Context passed to `DiscordOpsAlert` is redacted: sensitive keys (`password`,
+  `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key` / `api-key` / `apikey`,
+  `webhook`) and `Bearer <...>` values become `[redacted]`; nested arrays are
+  redacted recursively and rendered as JSON. Payloads stay under 1800 characters.
+- Never log secrets or PII in any lane. Prefer IDs over raw payloads.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Env key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the default `stack` (test suite pins `daily`). |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Retention for the `daily` archive channel. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level for the `audit` channel. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Retention for the `audit` channel. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | _(empty)_ | Discord incoming webhook URL. Empty means alerts are a silent no-op. |
+
+Example:
+
+```php
+use App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert;
+use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;
+
+// Archive (default)
+Log::info('Ticket issued', ['queue_id' => $queue->id]);
+
+// Audit (durable trail)
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Membership role changed', [
+    'actor_id' => $actor->id,
+    'entity_id' => $entity->id,
+    'new_role' => 'admin',
+]);
+
+// Alert (page a human)
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Asaas webhook failing',
+    'Signature verification failed 5 times in 10 minutes.',
+    ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks', 'entity_id' => $entity->id],
+);
+```
